==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*atro-eks}}, from root {{m|ine-pro||*h₁eh₂tro-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*eh₂ter-||fire}} (whence Avestan {{term|𐬁𐬙𐬀𐬭𐬱||fire|tr=ātarš|lang=ae}}, Umbrian {{term|tr=atru|lang=xum|sc=Ital}}, Oscan {{term|tr=Aadíriis|lang=osc|sc=Ital}}, Irish {{term|áith||kiln|lang=ga}}) + {{m|ine-pro||*h₃kʷós}}, {{m|ine-pro|*h₃ekʷ-||eye; to see}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈa.troːks/|lang=la}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-3rd-1E|atrōx|atrocis|atrōcis}}

# [[fierce]], [[savage]], [[bloody]]
